      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable that you feel that way when the fundamental structure of your life has dissolved; the loss of purpose feels like a mathematical impossibility. Therapy isn't about magically fixing the equation, but rather about helping you find a new framework to look at the zero. It's a process of acknowledging the void rather than trying to fill it instantly. Allow yourself the space to explore what might replace that old, rigid logic, even if it's just for a moment.",
      "source": "target",
